{
  "asset": "Pump P-201 - Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531 (diaphragm leaking chemical at the head, about 2 drops/s; motor running normally)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Diaphragm leak at the head, about 2 drops per second: no documented leak-rate limit for the Velatek VX-90 is in the evidence. The only manufacturer limits provided are for the AquaDyne HF-300 centrifugal pump (shaft seal, bearings, vibration) and do not apply to this asset. The leak cannot be graded against a limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Motor reported as running normally, but no vibration or bearing temperature readings were taken. The site stop rule (vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone) and the P1 rule (bearing temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit) cannot be applied. No VX-90 limits are available, and the HF-300 zones (Zone D above 7.1 mm/s RMS) and temperatures (alarm 80 C, trip 90 C) do not apply to this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before any work, raise the SSP-07 controls on the permit. SSP-07 applies to all pumps on site, and the work order must list every applicable control.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for all work on the leaking head and the dosed line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate the pump electrically at the MCC and apply lock-out/tag-out.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves. Under the line-break permit, drain and vent the pump head before opening it.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do NOT use the AquaDyne HF-300 seal procedure (5.2), the Table 5 torques or SB-2026-014 torques on this pump. They are for a different make and model. Obtain the Velatek VX-90 manual for the diaphragm replacement procedure and the head bolt torques before dismantling.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC. This is required for any work inside a pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "A line-break permit is required. Drain and vent first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves, because this is work on a chemically dosed line (the pump is reported leaking chemical).",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 Rev 3 applies to all pumps on site, including P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C14"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The AquaDyne HF-300 O&M manual (parts list, troubleshooting, procedures, Table 5 torques, vibration zones and temperature limits) covers the AquaDyne HF-300 centrifugal pump. P-201 is a Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531, so none of this content applies to the asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) applies only to HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 and above. Serial VX-5531 is not an HF3 serial and the pump is a different make, so neither the bulletin nor the Table 5 torques it supersedes apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 lists only P-101 to P-106 as chemically dosed (sodium hypochlorite), and P-201 is not listed. However, the fault report states that P-201 is a dosing pump leaking chemical, so the chemical-line PPE control has been applied as the conservative choice.",
      "citations": [
        "C16",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What chemical does P-201 dose, and is its safety data sheet available? Additional PPE or spill containment may be needed beyond goggles and nitrile gloves.",
